cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "CrooksJarzynskiLean: a Lean 4 formalization of the Crooks and Jarzynski fluctuation theorems"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "kiyo-e"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kiyo-e/CrooksJarzynskiLean"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-08-26"
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formal verification
  - stochastic thermodynamics
  - fluctuation theorems
  - Crooks theorem
  - Jarzynski equality
  - continuous-time Markov chains
  - matrix exponential semigroup
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked development of stochastic thermodynamics in Lean 4. In
  discrete time it proves finite-horizon Crooks and Jarzynski theorems for
  arbitrary measurable state spaces directly with Mathlib measures and Markov
  kernels, specializes them to Gibbs measures and standard physical work and
  free-energy weights, and provides real-integral, work-distribution,
  average-work second-law, non-atomic Gaussian, Metropolis–Hastings, and
  finite-state specializations. It also formalizes an explicit physical
  time-reversal protocol, compares discrete-time work conventions, and proves a
  path-uniform O(1/N) refinement bound. In continuous time it develops a
  finite-jump path space with segment-indexed factorized path densities and
  piecewise-constant rate factors on jump sectors, constructs a nonzero
  reversal-invariant fixed-horizon simplex reference measure with free-coordinate
  volume 1/n!, and derives fixed-sector, all-sector and fixed-horizon Crooks and
  Jarzynski theorems from local detailed balance. For the symmetric unit-rate
  two-state chain it proves normalization, Poisson jump-count masses and
  non-explosion, identifies the fixed-initial terminal marginals with the rows of
  the matrix exponential exp(TQ), and packages them as a Mathlib Markov kernel
  satisfying Chapman–Kolmogorov. An asymmetric reversible two-state chain
  followed by an energy quench supplies the physical layer: Gibbs equilibrium,
  partition functions, free-energy difference, real work, physical Crooks and
  Jarzynski relations, work-distribution Crooks, a strict second law, and the
  entropy-production integral fluctuation theorem. A general finite-state jump
  generator layer packages nonnegative rates into a conservative generator with a
  fixed-horizon counting reference; its fixed-initial path laws are proved
  non-explosive, their terminal marginals are identified with the rows of exp(TQ)
  and packaged as a Chapman–Kolmogorov Markov kernel, path concatenation gives a
  path-level Chapman–Kolmogorov identity, and every finite-dimensional marginal
  is identified with the chronological transition-kernel chain with
  matrix-exponential product atoms, instantiated on a branching three-state
  chain. A finite-window piecewise-constant driven protocol built from these
  path laws is concatenated into global real-time path laws carrying physical
  Crooks, Jarzynski, work-distribution, and average-work second-law theorems.
  No sorry placeholders or custom axioms.
